r-async","description":"Asynchronously read and write Unix archive files.","version":"0.1.3","homepage":"https://github.com/JayCanuck/node-ar-async","author":{"name":"Jason Robitaille","email":"jason@canuckcoding.ca"},"licenses":[{"type":"MIT","url":"https://github.com/JayCanuck/node-ar-async/blob/master/LICENSE"}],"main":"ar.js","repository":{"type":"git","url":"https://github.com/JayCanuck/node-ar-async.git"},"keywords":["ar"],"gitHead":"f9e5766965ba30426f9c206942f9326ffc6cc012","bugs":{"url":"https://github.com/JayCanuck/node-ar-async/issues"},"_id":"ar-async@0.1.3","scripts":{},"_shasum":"2e0485c011ff57e8eb922d34d5d76b96307c1b70","_from":"node-ar-async","_npmVersion":"1.4.28","_npmUser":{"name":"jaycanuck","email":"jason.robitaille@lge.com"},"maintainers":[{"name":"jaycanuck","email":"jason.robitaille@lge.com"}],"dist":{"shasum":"2e0485c011ff57e8eb922d34d5d76b96307c1b70","tarball":"https://registry.npmjs.org/ar-async/-/ar-async-0.1.3.tgz","integrity":"sha512-8CK91l7Ay+T24tcfX1mBs9i42k2lV8NSuT8QnGFVVMd9IexyKs/71PDnYErekgvGKPnRRAzmnNis43isW4Kqlw==","signatures":[{"keyid":"SHA256:jl3bwswu80PjjokCgh0o2w5c2U4LhQAE57gj9cz1kzA","sig":"MEUCIHotgNLGXxOQKanSN+wGhC/mfHq5QmFvDKFftqqac2crAiEAitNZuPXYesNVKDcF4X2t9iX1tJfV0EReKiWeZJU1LLg="}]}},"0.1.4":{"name":"ar-async","description":"Asynchronously read and write Unix archive files.","version":"0.1.4","homepage":"https://github.com/JayCanuck/node-ar-async","author":{"name":"Jason Robitaille","email":"jason@canuckcoding.ca"},"licenses":[{"type":"MIT","url":"https://github.com/JayCanuck/node-ar-async/blob/master/LICENSE"}],"main":"ar.js","repository":{"type":"git","url":"https://github.com/JayCanuck/node-ar-async.git"},"keywords":["ar"],"gitHead":"cd5fa957b30db58d660d3f51bc64f16ab688c162","bugs":{"url":"https://github.com/JayCanuck/node-ar-async/issues"},"_id":"ar-async@0.1.4","scripts":{},"_shasum":"92f76d625323ac0d2a2deb899c27b10fc9cea0e0","_from":"node-ar-async","_npmVersion":"1.4.28","_npmUser":{"name":"jaycanuck","email":"jason@canuckcoding.ca"},"maintainers":[{"name":"jaycanuck","email":"jason.robitaille@lge.com"}],"dist":{"shasum":"92f76d625323ac0d2a2deb899c27b10fc9cea0e0","tarball":"https://registry.npmjs.org/ar-async/-/ar-async-0.1.4.tgz","integrity":"sha512-iuFSHl96gQAStEPK457rAqVX0n5CVWrnE7SPdc/yS0ixkQXRd6h9W+8TJ1IA0sqgLolIO3oudpG8jl033GAiNg==","signatures":[{"keyid":"SHA256:jl3bwswu80PjjokCgh0o2w5c2U4LhQAE57gj9cz1kzA","sig":"MEUCIG4Bz4EiTLscc8VvViXc7QS3P6ve1IJSqC8FolJAHd4/AiEA11gJDVCYGsTVFd200ND/whwzIFADeBQ6PeWgrg921Gc="}]}}},"readme":"ar\n====\n\nA Node library for asynchronously reading and writing [Unix archive files](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ar_%28Unix%29). Currents supprts basic `ar` format, as well as BSD and GNU variants.\n\n###ArReader\n```javascript\nvar ar = require('ar'),\n    fs = require('fs'),\n    path = require('path');\n\n// extracts all of the files in \"some_archive.a\" to the folder \"./output\".\nvar outputDir = \"./output\";\nif (!fs.existsSync(outputDir)) fs.mkdirSync(outputDir);\n\nvar reader = new ar.ArReader(\"some_archive.a\");\nreader.on(\"open\", function() {\n\t// archive opened\n});\nreader.on(\"entry\", function(entry, next) {\n\t// entry is an instance of ArEntry\n\tvar name = entry.fileName();\n\tentry.fileData()\n\t\t.pipe(fs.createWriteStream(name))\n\t\t.on(\"finish\", next);\t\t\n});\nreader.on(\"error\", function(err) {\n\t// archive reading error\n});\nreader.on(\"end\", function() {\n\t// archive parsing ended\n});\nreader.on(\"close\", function() {\n\t// archive closed\n});\n```\n\nArReader automatically detects and handles BSD and GNU variant formats. All events are optional, so you only have to listen for the ones you want.\n\n###ArWriter\n```javascript\nvar ar = require('ar'),\n    fs = require('fs'),\n    path = require('path');\n\n// write files into a new ar archive at \"some_archive.a\"\n// in the case, specifies gnu variant format for long filenames\nvar writer = new ar.ArWriter(\"./some_archive.a\", {variant:\"gnu\"});\nwriter.writeEntries([\n\t\t\"./some_file\",\n\t\t\"./some_other_file\",\n\t\t\"./yet_another_file\"\n\t], function() {\n\t\t// optional callback after completion\n\t});\nwriter.on(\"open\", function() {\n\t// archive opened\n});\nwriter.on(\"entry\", function(entry) {\n\t// entry is an instance of ArEntry\n\t// signifies an entry has been written\n\t// unlike ArReader, there is no next function\n});\nwriter.on(\"error\", function(err) {\n\t// archive writing error\n});\nwriter.on(\"finish\", function() {\n\t// archive writing ended and closed\n});\n```\n\nArWriter by default will truncate filenames at 16 bytes long. For long file names, specify a variant format, like done above. Currently \"GNU\" and \"BSD\" are supported. Additionally, you can specify \"uid\", \"gid\", and \"mode\" number values in the options json; they will override the values for each file written. All events are optional, so you only have to listen for the ones you want.\n\n###ArEntry\nSee ar.js for inline ArEntry documention, but here are the key APIs\n\n* [ArEntry].fileName() - String - Filename of the file in the entry\n* [ArEntry].fileSize() - Number - Number of bytes the file takes up\n* [ArEntry].fileData() - Stream - Readable stream for file data\n* [ArEntry].date() - Date - Last modified date of the file\n* [ArEntry].uid() - Number - UID of the file\n* [ArEntry].gid() - Number - GID of the file\n* [ArEntry].mode() - Number - File mode\n\n###License\nLicensed under the MIT License (MIT)\n\nnode-ar-async Copyright (c) 2014 Jason Robitaille.\nhttps://github.com/JayCanuck/node-ar-async\n\nBased on, and including code from, from node-ar, Copyright (c) 2013 John Vilk.\nhttps://github.com/jvilk/node-ar\n\n","maintainers":[{"name":"jaycanuck","email":"jason.robitaille@lge.com"}],"time":{"modified":"2022-06-13T03:20:30.890Z","created":"2014-11-13T07:51:17.528Z","0.1.0":"2014-11-13T07:51:17.528Z","0.1.1":"2014-11-15T13:16:54.395Z","0.1.2":"2014-11-15T14:30:25.373Z","0.1.3":"2014-11-15T14:52:58.337Z"